page /guides/brass-care
  text
    title "Caring for brass"
    body  "Brass darkens with time. Wipe it with a soft dry cloth each month. To bring back the shine, use a little brass polish on a cloth, never on the lamp, and buff it off. Do not use water near the switch or the socket."

page /guides/choosing-bulbs
  text
    title "Choosing a bulb"
    body  "Every Bench lamp takes an E27 bulb. Warm bulbs of 2200 to 2700 kelvin suit living rooms; 4000 kelvin suits desks and studios. Use a dimmable bulb with a dimmer switch, and keep within the wattage printed under the shade."

page /guides/rewiring
  text
    title "Rewiring an old lamp"
    body  "Unplug the lamp first. Take off the shade and the bulb, then the socket cover. Note which wire goes where before you undo them. Use a new cord of the same rating, and ask an electrician if you are unsure."

page /guides/placing-lights
  text
    title "Placing lights in a room"
    body  "Light a room in three layers: a ceiling or pendant light for the whole room, floor and table lamps for corners, and a task light where you read or work. Keep bulbs below eye level when you sit."

page /guides/outdoor-use
  text
    title "Using lamps outdoors"
    body  "Only the lantern is made for outdoor use. Keep every other lamp indoors and dry. Charge the lantern fully before its first use, and bring it inside in frost."

page /guides/dimmers
  text
    title "Dimmers and switches"
    body  "The desk lamp has a dimmer in its base. Other lamps work with a plug-in dimmer between the plug and the socket. Wall dimmers need a dimmable bulb and a compatible dimmer rated for low loads."

page /guides/energy
  text
    title "Saving energy"
    body  "A filament LED bulb uses about a tenth of the power of an old bulb and lasts ten years. Turn lamps off at the switch when you leave, and use the sleep timer on the night light."

page /guides/moving-house
  text
    title "Packing lamps to move"
    body  "Take the bulb and shade off, wrap the base in a towel and pack the shade on its own. Never pack a shade under heavy boxes. Keep the screws of a wall lamp in a bag taped to its arm."

page /guides/kids-safety
  text
    title "Lamps and children"
    body  "Keep cords out of reach and use the cord clips we send with every lamp. The night light stays cool to the touch. Do not leave a clip lamp on a bunk while a child sleeps."

page /guides/repairs
  text
    title "Repairs and spare parts"
    body  "We sell every part of every lamp: sockets, switches, cords, shades and bases. Write to us with a photo and the lamp's name, and we send the part or take the lamp in for repair."

page /help/shipping
  faq
    title "Shipping"
    item "Do you ship abroad?"
      text "Yes, to most countries, in five to ten working days."
    item "How much is shipping?"
      text "Shipping is free over 80 dollars, and 6 dollars below."
    item "Can I track my parcel?"
      text "Yes, the email we send when it leaves has a tracking link."
    item "Do you ship to post office boxes?"
      text "Yes, except for floor lamps, which need a street address."
    item "Can I change my address after ordering?"
      text "Yes, until the parcel leaves; write to us with your order number."

page /help/returns
  faq
    title "Returns"
    item "Can I return a lamp?"
      text "Yes, within 30 days, unused and in its box."
    item "Who pays for returns?"
      text "We do, with the label in the box."
    item "When do I get my money back?"
      text "Within five working days of the lamp reaching us."
    item "Can I exchange a lamp for another?"
      text "Yes, tell us which one and we send it when yours arrives."
    item "Can I return a spare shade?"
      text "Yes, like any lamp, within 30 days."

page /help/warranty
  faq
    title "Warranty"
    item "Is there a warranty?"
      text "Every lamp has a two-year warranty."
    item "What does the warranty cover?"
      text "Faults in parts and wiring, not wear or damage."
    item "Are bulbs under warranty?"
      text "Bulbs have their own one-year warranty."
    item "How do I claim?"
      text "Write to us with a photo and your order number."
    item "Can I extend the warranty?"
      text "Yes, to five years, for 15 dollars a lamp."

page /help/payments
  faq
    title "Payments"
    item "Which cards do you take?"
      text "Every major credit and debit card."
    item "Can I pay later?"
      text "Yes, in three parts with no fee."
    item "Do you send invoices?"
      text "Yes, every order email has its invoice."
    item "Can I pay by bank transfer?"
      text "Yes, for orders over 500 dollars."
    item "Is my payment safe?"
      text "Yes, we never see or keep your card number."

page /help/trade
  faq
    title "Trade and bulk orders"
    item "Do you sell to shops?"
      text "Yes, write to us for the trade price list."
    item "Is there a discount for many lamps?"
      text "Ten percent off ten lamps or more."
    item "Can you make a custom colour?"
      text "Yes, for fifty lamps or more."
    item "How long do bulk orders take?"
      text "Four to six weeks."
    item "Do you supply hotels?"
      text "Yes, with hardwired wall and pendant lamps."

page /help/gifts
  faq
    title "Gifts"
    item "Do you sell gift cards?"
      text "Yes, from 25 to 500 dollars."
    item "Can you wrap a gift?"
      text "Yes, in recycled paper, for 3 dollars."
    item "Can I hide the price?"
      text "Yes, gift orders carry no price."
    item "Can I send a note?"
      text "Yes, we print it on a card in the box."
    item "Do gift cards expire?"
      text "No, never."

page /help/account
  faq
    title "Your account"
    item "Do I need an account to order?"
      text "No, you can order as a guest."
    item "How do I reset my password?"
      text "Use the link on the sign-in page."
    item "Can I see my old orders?"
      text "Yes, on your account page."
    item "How do I delete my account?"
      text "Write to us and we delete it within a week."
    item "Do you send newsletters?"
      text "Only if you ask for them, once a month."

page /help/electrics
  faq
    title "Plugs and electrics"
    item "Which plug does my lamp have?"
      text "The plug of the country you order from."
    item "Can I use a lamp abroad?"
      text "Yes, with a plug adapter; every lamp takes 100 to 240 volts."
    item "Can a wall lamp be hardwired?"
      text "Yes, with the hardwire kit, by an electrician."
    item "What cable length do lamps have?"
      text "Two metres, and three for the floor lamp."
    item "Are your lamps certified?"
      text "Yes, every lamp is tested and certified."

page /pricing
  pricing cards
    title    "Care plans"
    currency usd
    plan "Basic"
      monthly 3
      annual  30
      cta     "Start" /contact
    plan "Plus"
      monthly 6
      annual  60
      cta     "Start" /contact

page /about
  text
    title "About Bench"
    body  "Bench is a workshop of six people in an old mill. We have made lamps since 2014, by hand, from brass, walnut and stoneware."

page /contact
  hero center
    title "Write to us"
    sub   "We answer within a working day."
    cta   "Email us" mailto:hello@bench.example

page /stores
  text
    title "Where to see our lamps"
    body  "Our lamps are on show in our workshop in the old mill, open Saturdays from ten to four, and in twelve shops we list on request."

page /careers
  text
    title "Work with us"
    body  "We hire a maker each spring. Write to us with photos of things you have made."

page /press
  text
    title "Press"
    body  "Photos and the story of the workshop are free to use with credit. Write to us for samples."

page /sustainability
  text
    title "Materials and waste"
    body  "Our brass is recycled, our walnut comes from fallen trees and our boxes are paper only. We repair rather than replace."
